Files are in wsv format. First line is header:
# lambda[um] m_real m_imaginary
Following lines are three columns that follow 
header.

Key:
ri-du_v15_6.wsv       - This is equivalent to Colarco et al. 2014
                        (equivalent to what is used in GEOS and GEFS, 
                        and similar to whatis used in ModelE for SW)
ri-du_woodward.wsv    - This is from Woodward 2001 (used in IFS model)
ri-du_balkanski.wsv   - This is the 1.5% hematite model from Balkanski 
                        et al. 2007 and used in UM and MONARCH (SW only)
ri-du_balkanski27.wsv - This is the 2.7% hematite model from Balkanski 
                        et al. 2007 and used in AM4
miam00                - This is differently formatted provided by OPAC
                        and what is used in MONARCH (LW only), SILAM,
                        MASINGAR and NAAPS. Look at last two columns
                        for nref


